.TH CHTTPCLI_CONSTRUCT_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_construct_scoped \- declare and initialize a chttpcli handle that the library destroys automatically
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

chttpcli_construct_scoped(name)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro is chttpcli_declare_scoped followed by chttpclient_create.
It declares name with the GCC cleanup attribute, calls
chttpclient_create and stores the result in name, so the client is
destroyed automatically when name leaves the scope. If the creation
fails, the macro calls _ccol_fatal_err() and does not return.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name     The identifier of the new handle variable.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_construct (3),
.BR chttpcli_declare_scoped (3)
